&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is committed to complying with applicable data privacy and security laws and regulations. For more information, please see our Personnel and Job Candidate Privacy Notice at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/legal/personnel-policy/&quot;&gt;https://www.okta.com/legal/personnel-policy/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Every Identity, from AI to Human&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Identity is the key to unlocking the potential of AI. Okta secures AI by building the trusted, neutral infrastructure that enables organizations to safely embrace this new era. This work requires a relentless drive to solve complex challenges with real-world stakes. We are looking for builders and owners who operate with speed and urgency and execute with excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an opportunity to do career-defining work. We&#39;re all in on this mission. If you are too, let&#39;s talk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced &lt;strong&gt;EMEA Benefits Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to oversee and optimize our regional benefit programs. Based in Dublin and reporting to our US-based leadership, you will lead the implementation, day-to-day administration, and compliance of Okta&#39;s Total Rewards offerings across the EMEA region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a data-driven problem solver with strong business acumen, capable of translating complex data into financial projections and actionable strategy. You must be an execution-focused leader who excels at managing multiple deadlines, building cross-functional relationships, and influencing stakeholders at all levels of a global, matrixed organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep Regional Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the subject matter expert for complex, region-specific programs, particularly focusing on pension governance, healthcare trusts, and employee councils across EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Procurement &amp;amp; Governance:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the full vendor lifecycle for regional insurance carriers, brokers, and third-party administrators. Lead comprehensive onboarding, overseeing contract negotiations, security protocols, and data privacy reviews, while driving ongoing accountability through SLAs and Quarterly Business Reviews (QBRs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Administration &amp;amp; Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage the end-to-end administration of health, retirement, and wellbeing initiatives. Drive seamless data exchange between vendors, payroll, and internal HR platforms to minimize administrative friction and maximize data integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance, Risk &amp;amp; Benchmarking:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactively monitor the EMEA regulatory landscape and conduct regular audits to ensure strict compliance with local laws. Conduct regional market research to ensure offerings remain highly competitive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with EMEA Payroll, People Operations (POPS), Finance, and Legal to ensure flawless program delivery, accurate taxation, and cohesive alignment across G&amp;amp;A functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data &amp;amp; AI Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Utilize Workday and ServiceNow to track and report on key metrics. Leverage AI tools to analyze plan utilization, forecast costs, and personalize employee communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Evolution:&lt;/strong&gt; Challenge the status quo to streamline administrative burdens. Document, implement, and automate processes in close partnership with the People Operations team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Experience &amp;amp; Escalations:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the highest level of regional escalation for complex benefits inquiries, ensuring a high-touch, empathetic, and seamless experience for Okta employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a subject matter expert for the People &amp;amp; Places community, managers, and employees, ensuring clear, effective delivery of benefit updates and educational resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Strategy Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain the team’s global project portfolio via SmartSheets and assist with overarching global rewards strategy initiatives as required, ensuring EMEA is represented in global design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring to the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Degree in a related discipline with 8+ years of experience in a regional Benefits role within a multinational environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; In-depth knowledge of complex benefits regulations, labor laws, and tax compliance across the EMEA region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical &amp;amp; Financial Rigor:&lt;/strong&gt; A metrics-focused mindset with the ability to interpret quantitative/qualitative data, project financial impacts, and translate insights into actionable business recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution &amp;amp; Project Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Highly execution-driven with the ability to manage multiple, deadline-focused initiatives with high precision and autonomy in a dynamic, fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relationship Building &amp;amp; Influence:&lt;/strong&gt; A track record of building trust across a matrixed organization, with the communication skills to present information effectively and influence diverse stakeholders at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong command of Google Workspace and Workday, AI tools (i.e. Gemini, Notebook LM).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-RB4&lt;/p&gt;
