&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual base salary range for this position for candidates located in the San Francisco Bay area is between:  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$258,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$355,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Below is the annual base salary range for candidates located in California (excluding San Francisco Bay Area), Colorado, Illinois, New York and Washington. Your actual base salary will depend on factors such as your skills, qualifications, experience, and work location. In addition, Okta offers equity (where applicable), bonus, and benefits, including health, dental and vision insurance, 401(k), flexible spending account, and paid leave (including PTO and parental leave) in accordance with our applicable plans and policies. To learn more about our Total Rewards program please visit: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://rewards.okta.com/us&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;https://rewards.okta.com/us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual base salary range for this position for candidates located in California (excluding San Francisco Bay Area), Colorado, Illinois, New York, and Washington is between:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$230,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$317,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Okta Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://rewards.okta.com&quot;&gt;Supporting Your Well-Being&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/okta-for-good/&quot;&gt;Driving Social Impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/talent-connection-community/&quot;&gt;Developing Talent and Fostering Connection + Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is committed to complying with applicable data privacy and security laws and regulations. For more information, please see our Personnel and Job Candidate Privacy Notice at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/legal/personnel-policy/&quot;&gt;https://www.okta.com/legal/personnel-policy/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Every Identity, from AI to Human&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Identity is the key to unlocking the potential of AI. Okta secures AI by building the trusted, neutral infrastructure that enables organizations to safely embrace this new era. This work requires a relentless drive to solve complex challenges with real-world stakes. We are looking for builders and owners who operate with speed and urgency and execute with excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an opportunity to do career-defining work. We&#39;re all in on this mission. If you are too, let&#39;s talk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Auth0, an Okta company, is the leading customer identity platform for developers. Our mission is to secure the world’s identities so innovators can innovate. As AI reshapes how applications are built and used, identity and security are becoming critical to enabling safe and trusted agentic experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking an experienced and visionary product leader to serve as Director of Product Management for Auth0’s AI portfolio, focused on Auth0 for AI Agents. You will define and execute a strategy that builds on Auth0’s momentum in identity and security for AI agents, helping developers and organizations from fast-growing AI-native startups to large enterprises deliver secure and scalable agentic applications with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define and Own the AI Product and Partnership Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and execute the strategy for Auth0’s AI portfolio, with a focus on Auth0 for AI Agents. Identify high-impact opportunities and ecosystem partnerships that expand reach, accelerate adoption, and deliver differentiated value to developers and enterprises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a Founder and a Scaler:&lt;/strong&gt; Bring a &quot;0-to-1&quot; entrepreneurial mindset to define, experiment, and launch new products, combined with the experience to scale them into mature, widely adopted solutions. Balance agility and innovation with the structure and discipline required for long-term success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and Grow the PM Team:&lt;/strong&gt; Mentor and manage a team of product managers, fostering a culture of innovation, accountability, and customer focus. Provide direction, coaching, and career development to scale impact across the portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engage with Customers and the Developer Community:&lt;/strong&gt; Build strong relationships with customers, partners, and developers to uncover needs, validate solutions, and ensure Auth0 for AI Agents delivers meaningful value in real-world use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Product Delivery and Differentiation:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with engineering, design, and external collaborators to deliver secure, scalable, and developer-friendly solutions that address the unique challenges of agentic applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion Ecosystem Standards and Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Shape and influence emerging standards in identity and AI, including agent-to-agent (A2A) communication and Model Context Protocol (MCP). Represent Auth0 as a thought leader with industry groups and the developer community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Cross-Functional Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with GTM teams (Product Marketing, Sales, Developer Marketing, and Developer Relations) to ensure successful launches, enablement, and measurable adoption of Auth0’s AI offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10+ years of product management experience&lt;/strong&gt;, including at least 2+ years in a Director-level or equivalent leadership role, with a significant focus on B2B SaaS and developer-facing products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep technical acumen and hands-on developer credibility&lt;/strong&gt;: Strong understanding of identity protocols (OAuth, OIDC, SAML), APIs, AI frameworks, and the emerging agent ecosystem. Ability to write code and work directly with APIs, SDKs, and sample applications to prototype and validate developer workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven “0-to-1” and scaling experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated success in building and launching new products, programs, or business lines from scratch, and scaling them into durable, widely adopted solutions. Startup founder or early-stage employee experience is a significant plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional product instincts:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to deeply understand developer needs and translate them into compelling, integrated product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; A dual-threat leader who is as comfortable diving into technical details as they are in developing and executing a go-to-market growth strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership and Influence:&lt;/strong&gt; The ability to lead through influence in a highly matrixed organization, working effectively with product, engineering, marketing, and sales leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent Communication Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; The ability to articulate a complex strategy and vision to diverse audiences, from C-level executives to developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4058&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Passion for AI and identity:&lt;/strong&gt; A genuine enthusiasm for the potential of AI and a deep, demonstrable interest in the future of identity and security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;Okta’s Top 5 Core Leadership Competencies are part of the deeply ingrained principles that guide all of our company’s actions. They also align strongly to our cultural cornerstones, our Okta values: love our customers, empower our people, never stop innovating, act with integrity, and maintain transparency. It’s our expectation that our managers and leaders embody these core competencies:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Builds Effective Teams: Building strong-identity teams that apply their diverse skills and perspectives to achieve common goals.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Demonstrates Self-Awareness (EQ): Using a combination of feedback and reflection to gain productive insight into personal strengths and weaknesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Develops Talent: Developing people to meet both their career goals and the organization’s goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Drives Results: Consistently achieving results, even under tough circumstances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Strategic Mindset: Seeing ahead to future possibilities and translating them into breakthrough strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;**You must attend in person onboarding in the San Francisco office the first week.&lt;/p&gt;
